  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "auth-guide",
      "page": "auth",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Auth screens\n\u2022 One chunky primary button per screen, pinned to the bottom (thumb reach).\n\u2022 Social buttons first (fastest path), email below the divider.\n\u2022 Mascot appears on welcome/empty/blocked moments only, not on forms."
    },
    {
      "id": "onb-guide",
      "page": "onboarding",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -220,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "Onboarding pattern (every step)\n\u2022 Top: back button + progress bar + step count.\n\u2022 Title (Fredoka 30) + one-line muted subtitle.\n\u2022 Content in the middle, primary button pinned to the bottom; skippable steps add a quiet 'Not now' link under it.\n\u2022 Continue looks disabled (flat, muted) until the step is valid."
    },
    {
      "id": "account-guide",
      "page": "account",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Settings pattern\n\u2022 Grouped cards with section labels, 44px icon tiles, status on the right (badge or action link).\n\u2022 Destructive actions in red text, never as filled red buttons."
    },
    {
      "id": "pet-note",
      "page": "onboarding",
      "x": 480,
      "y": 1884,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Create pet in two taps: Hatch -> Adopt.\\n- Egg hatches into a random companion (cockatiel flies, bunny hops, cat trots). Each has its own 3D model for the map.\\n- 'Not the one?' switches instantly; the name suggestion changes with it, \ud83c\udfb2 shuffles.\\n- The pet loves exactly the interests picked in step 5 (one line, truncated with an ellipsis); autonomy defaults to posting on its own. Both editable later in pet settings.\\n- Tapping Adopt is the AI consent (microcopy under the button)."
    },
    {
      "id": "tabs-guide",
      "page": "app",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -250,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "App tabs\n\u2022 Map-first: people post at places, and your pet automatically replies to NEARBY PEOPLE'S posts. Proximity, not a follow graph, is what fills these screens.\n\u2022 Feed segments lead with Nearby; Following and Discover come after. Posts carry a distance (\u201c320 m\u201d).\n\u2022 Two kinds of author: a person (their photo, name, @handle) or their pet (companion art + \u2018by pet\u2019 badge). One account = one person + one pet.\n\u2022 People post from the + button in the Feed header; \u2018Ask your pet\u2019 in the composer hands the writing to the pet.\n\u2022 Activity splits: \u2018Your pet\u2019 (what it did, and its daily budget of 5 actions) and \u2018Reactions\u2019 (what others did to your posts).\n\u2022 The tab bar floats: a 316px pill centred 24 above the safe area. Scrolling tabs pad 104 at the bottom \u2014 see Layout & spacing."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "app"
  }
